threads.body:
The `**Span kind`/`**Span status` guards below let a span inline that prose in its `note` instead. When it does, the prose renders as part of `note` -- ahead of the span name -- and the generated line is suppressed. So the span name lands in a different spot per span:

- `gen_ai.inference.client` (inlines kind): kind -> **Span name** -> status
- `mcp.server` (inlines status): status -> **Span name** -> kind
- `invoke_agent` (inlines neither): **Span name** -> kind -> status

Emitting `name.note` before `note` puts it in the same place everywhere. Needs a `make generate-all`.

```suggestion
{%- if span.name and span.name.note %}

{{ span.name.note | trim }}{% endif %}
{%- if span.note %}

{{ span.note | trim }}{% endif %}
{%- if "**Span kind" not in (span.note or "") %}

**Span kind** SHOULD be `{{ span.kind | upper }}`.{% endif %}
```

